 "id": "story-2-prod-command",
 "name": "Story 2: production command requests, made rarer and safer",
 "description": "People ask me to run commands on production bastions. Agents explain the command from runbooks, check the authority chain (asking back when it is missing, which teaches requesters the process), and gather context, including repeats needed in other environments. I decide and run it; nobody else can. Every case is logged; patterns and incidents become problem statements and proposals, which the company adopts faster with more evidence and right after an incident. Runbooks learn from every case and incident and go stale on their own. Time unit: a working hour; horizon 26 weeks.",
 "time_unit": "working hour",
 "horizon": 1040,
 "dt": 0.25,
